# <Site Name> — Claude Code Config

> A static site. Rules: `AGENTS.md`. Facts about this site: `SSOT.md`. The rules in
> `.claude/rules/` load by themselves while a matching file is in play.

---

## Project Snapshot

Next.js (App Router) + React, prerendered at build time. Mode: `<export | ssg-with-endpoints>`
(`scripts/check/site.config.json`). Production origin: `<https://www.example.com>`.
Dev: `npm run dev` · Build: `npm run build` · Serve the build: `npm run serve:build`

---

## Context Loading Strategy

| Task | Read |
| --- | --- |
| A new page or section | `SSOT.md` §2 (routes) + §4 (design) + `AGENTS.md` §B, §C |
| Metadata, sitemap, robots, share images, JSON-LD | `SSOT.md` §8 + `.claude/rules/web/seo.md` |
| Headers, CSP, third-party scripts | `SSOT.md` §5, §7 + `.claude/rules/web/security.md` |
| A form | `SSOT.md` §6 + `.claude/rules/web/forms-on-static-hosting.md` |
| Images, fonts, animation, a heavy hero | `SSOT.md` §9 + `.claude/rules/web/performance.md` |
| Translations | `.claude/rules/web/i18n.md` (when the site has more than one language) |
| Anything that looks like a known trap | `.claude/anti-patterns/INDEX.md` |

---

## Quality Gates

Before calling a task done, run `bash scripts/check/gates.sh`: the source gates `.husky/pre-commit`
runs too (format and lint, secrets, types, dead code, static-export, image and font budgets).

After a change to pages, content, images, fonts or headers, build and check the result:

```bash
npm run build
node scripts/check/site-audit.mjs   # sitemap, robots, metadata, share images, JSON-LD, links, budgets, headers
npm run check:a11y                  # a real browser: pa11y-ci or axe, when installed
npm run check:lighthouse            # Core Web Vitals budgets, when lighthouserc.json is installed
```

A check that fails is fixed, never silenced: no budget is raised and no rule disabled without the
user agreeing (`AGENTS.md` § G).

---

## Protected Files

```
.env*                         ← list with scripts/env/show.sh; change only while unlocked (docs/unlock.md)
AGENTS.md · SSOT.md           ← propose the change; the user makes it
public/_headers               ← the security headers the host sends; edits need the user's approval
scripts/check/site.config.json · lighthouserc.json ← budgets; edits need the user's approval
.claude/settings.json         ← permissions and sandbox; the hooks come from the installed plugins
.claude/agent-config-kit.lock ← written by setup and sync; its presence turns the plugins' hooks on
```

---

## Commit Format

```
type(scope): subject
```

Types: `feat` · `fix` · `refactor` · `chore` · `docs` · `style` · `perf` · `test`.

